<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leopoldina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1652</span> · Also known as German National Academy of Sciences Leopoldina</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Leopoldina is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s national academy of sciences, based in Halle. It was founded in 1652 in the imperial city of Schweinfurt by four physicians as the Academia Naturae Curiosorum and took its name from Emperor Leopold I, who granted it privileges in 1687. It was made the national academy in 2008.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leopoldina.jpg" alt="Leopoldina" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gunther Tschuch PaulT · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leopoldina_Halle_Jaegerberg2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
